// The in-thread collector: a whole body gathered into a String, as its pieces
// arrive on the thread that owns the connection (an HTTP client's 'get', a server's
// request body). The producer and the consumer are the same thread, so a hop to an
// actor per piece would buy nothing; this is the plain helper that does the limit
// check and the append, once, for every such site. Releasing the piece's credit to
// the connection stays with the caller, whose connection it is (the limit being
// passed is the caller's to cancel for). It saves no copy: the result must be
// contiguous.

// Appends 'piece' to 'body' unless that would make it longer than 'limit'. True
// when it was appended; false when it was not (the body is as it was, and the
// caller ends the transfer, once)
pub fn gather(body: &mut String, piece: &Array[u8], limit: usize) bool {
  if body.len() + piece.len() > limit {return false;}
  body.appendBytes(piece);
  true
}
